   "stem": {
      "text": "The function s is defined by s(x) = (2x + 1) / (x^2 + 2x - 15) for x >= -4 only. Find the largest interval that contains x = 0 on which s is continuous, name the reason, and give the number of integers that interval contains."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 7
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The denominator (x + 5)(x - 3) is zero at x = -5 and x = 3, and only x = 3 lies in the stated domain x >= -4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               5
            ],
