               "Subtract",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "A rational function is continuous at every input of its domain. On x >= -4 its domain is [-4, 3) U (3, infinity), and at x = -4 continuity is one sided from the right.",
         "mathjson": 3
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece containing x = 0 is [-4, 3), closed at the stated endpoint -4 and open at 3.",
         "mathjson": -4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The integers in [-4, 3) are -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1 and 2.",
         "mathjson": 7
